g**: `conditions`, `known_defects_acknowledged` and `declared_non_coverage_acknowledged` are all optional, so a disposition whose **name asserts conditions exist** required none, and UAT-I13's aggregate-burying was reachable one enum value over.\n\n**C enforces the precondition rather than withdrawing the judgement.** That is the right repair when a rationale is sound and unguarded, and it is the pattern worth reusing: a defence that names a field is a defence that the field must be non-empty.\n\n**C10 is the one that changes a promise into a mechanism.** UAT-I17 says a material change invalidates an acceptance. Until now that was prose. Recomputing the scenario-set digest means a scenario added or removed after an acceptance was issued **cannot carry that acceptance forward silently**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Each of C7–C11 refuses its violation, naming its invariant, and admits the corrected form.\n2. **Every control mutation-checked individually, with survivors reported as a deliverable** (#266 criterion 4), under the full protocol: `-B`, `__pycache__` cleared, **named negative control first**, `git checkout --` restore, **in-process liveness witness** per mutation, and **parser anti-vacuity** — the parsed test count must equal the module-declared count or the run exits before measuring.\n3. Untyped bindings remain admissible — additive, as B established.\n4. **Open-ended (#270):** enumerate the adjacent encodings of the same defect — every other `disposition` value, every other acknowledgement field, an empty-string condition, a condition naming a *different* scenario — and confirm none admits an unnamed critical failure. The defect this rung closes was reachable *one enum value over* from a control that looked complete; the same neighbourhood must be walked rather than assumed.\n5. No lifecycle change, no second gate (UAT-I20), no adapter registered.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nCross-evidence and cross-dossier checks · binding an acknowledgement to a defect *resolution* state (#266's own exclusion) · `badf-production-readiness`'s two G10 types · WP-UAT-D (shadow) and WP-UAT-E (admission).\n\n## Surfaces\n\n**Declared up front**, per the #264 lesson where a missing `expected_surfaces` cost a REV condition: `scripts/badf_gate.py`, `tests/test_badf_uat_evidence.py`, `docs/governance/GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md`, `badf/demands/BADF-DEM-0111.json`, `badf/skill-registry.json` if the rung status advances, plus the WP record and the gate-forced reconcile.\n\n**Version tier:** minor. **Shared-surface** (`badf_gate.py`) → **QA + REV**. Ids swept clean on all four surfaces at filing.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
